
Copilot Instructions for AI Coding Agents

Purpose:

Enable an AI agent to become productive quickly by listing where to look, canonical workflows, and repo-specific patterns.
Orientation (first 5 minutes):

Inspect root manifests: look for package.json, pyproject.toml, go.mod, pubspec.yaml, Makefile, Dockerfile.
Identify entry points and services: lib/, bin/, src/, cmd/, packages/, apps/.
Open CI: check .github/workflows/ and any ci/ directories.
Read README.md and CONTRIBUTING.md for human workflows.
Big-picture architecture (where to map):

Service boundaries: folders named api, server, worker, cron usually indicate separate processes.
Data flows: search for DB clients, HTTP servers/clients, message brokers (Kafka/RabbitMQ), and storage SDK usage to draw the graph.
Monorepo cues: presence of packages/, pnpm-workspace.yaml, lerna.json, or multiple pubspec.yaml files.
Canonical commands (find exact ones and prefer them):

Use scripts from manifests. Examples to search for and trust as canonical:
npm run build / npm test / npm start
python -m pytest, poetry run pytest
go test ./...
flutter run or dart run when pubspec.yaml exists
If ambiguous, use CI job steps from .github/workflows as the source of truth.
Project conventions & patterns to respect:

JavaScript/TypeScript: src/ → dist/; check tsconfig.json paths and scripts.
Dart/Flutter: single-app lib/main.dart or bin/; prefer flutter tooling if flutter appears in pubspec.yaml.
Go: binaries under cmd/<name>/.
Tests: run per-package tests in monorepos; do not assume a single root test command unless present.
Lint/format: check .eslintrc, analysis_options.yaml, or analysis_options in Dart for formatting rules.
Integration points to note:

Environment files: *.env, .env.example — list required vars.
Infra manifests: Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, k8s/, helm/.
External services: note usages of AWS/GCP/Azure SDKs, database drivers, or third-party APIs.
What an agent should produce here (concrete, replaceable content):

Top-level snapshot (3–6 lines): root build/test/run commands + main service folders.
Exact commands to run locally (copy-paste):
Build: npm run build or make build or flutter build
Test: npm test or pytest -q or flutter test
Start: npm start or docker-compose up --build or flutter run
Key files to inspect for changes: list 3–6 authoritative paths (e.g., package.json, pubspec.yaml, lib/main.dart, src/server/).
When changing code:

Make small, focused commits. Update affected README.md or pubspec.yaml/package.json scripts if behavior changes.
For monorepos, update both package-level and root workspace manifests.
Merging with existing instructions:

If this repo already has .github/copilot-instructions.md, merge by preserving any repo-specific commands, CI job names, and maintainer contacts.
If unclear:

Add a short repository snapshot at the top of this file listing the canonical: build, test, run commands and main service folders.
